% 4. cv2.ximgproc.anisotropicDiffusion
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% OPENCV: modules/ximgproc/src/anisodiff.cpp:242-291 (public entry
% anisotropicDiffusion(); the CPU iteration loop with temp0x/temp1x is :274-289) plus
% the per-row kernel class ADBody at :84-200; OpenCL path ocl_anisotropicDiffusion at
% :203-240 (its loop is :215-237). Header doc + declaration:
% modules/ximgproc/include/opencv2/ximgproc.hpp:216-236.
% DECLARED BY OpenCV: no cite key. The header states in prose "The function applies
%   Perona-Malik anisotropic diffusion to an image" and prints div(c grad I) with the
%   two conductivities c = exp(-(||grad I||/K)^2) "or" c = 1/(1+(||grad I||/K)^2)
%   (ximgproc.hpp:218-229). Neither Perona nor Malik appears anywhere in
%   opencv_contrib-5.0.0/modules/ximgproc/doc/ximgproc.bib or in
%   opencv-5.0.0/doc/opencv.bib, so the primary reference below is supplied by us.
% WHAT THE CODE ACTUALLY IS (verified in the source, not from the doc): scalar
%   Perona-Malik only, and only equation (1). ADBody::operator() (anisodiff.cpp:95-194)
%   loops over the 8 neighbours of a CV_8UC3 pixel (offset table tab[] at :100), forms
%   nabla = |d0|+|d1|+|d2| (L1 gradient summed over channels, :183), looks up
%   w = exptab[nabla] (:184; SIMD equivalent at :149-152) with exptab[k] =
%   exp(-(k/sigma)^2), sigma = K*cn*255 (:257-263), and writes
%   saturate_cast<uchar>(c + alpha*sum(w*delta)) (:189-191) -- i.e. an explicit
%   forward-Euler step whose state is re-quantised to 8 bits every iteration. There is
%   NO tensor: `grep -c -i "weickert|tensor|jmatrix|eigen" anisodiff.cpp` = 0, so this
%   is NOT Weickert-style structure-tensor diffusion and must not be described as such. The second
%   (rational) conductivity shown in the doc is not implemented -- confirmed
%   independently by the module author's comment on opencv/opencv_contrib#1573
%   (2019-11-07): "The diffusion method also does not support both equations for
%   c(x, y, t) mentioned in Perona and Malik's paper."
@article{perona1991diffusion,
  author  = {Perona, Pietro and Malik, Jitendra},
  title   = {Scale-Space and Edge Detection Using Anisotropic Diffusion},
  journal = {IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence},
  volume  = {12},
  number  = {7},
  pages   = {629--639},
  year    = {1990},
  doi     = {10.1109/34.56205}
}
% VERIFY: GET api.crossref.org/works/10.1109/34.56205 -> title "Scale-space and edge
%   detection using anisotropic diffusion"; IEEE TPAMI; volume 12; issue 7; pages
%   629-639; issued AND published-print = [1990, 7]; authors P. Perona / J. Malik.
%   doi.org content negotiation returns the same: "Perona, P., & Malik, J. (1990).
%   ... IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence, 12(7), 629-639."
% DISCREPANCY, reported rather than papered over: the task brief expected
%   "TPAMI 13(7):679-699, 1991". No identifier we can reach supports that. The page
%   range 629-639 is corroborated by an independent implementation (Peter Kovesi's
%   anisodiff.m header cites "IEEE TPAMI 12(7):629-639, July 1990"), but the volume and
%   year are inconsistent across sources: the registered DOI record says vol 12 / 1990,
%   while the paper is commonly cited as vol 13 / 1991. The alternative DOI often seen,
%   10.1109/26.86568, does NOT resolve: GET api.crossref.org/works/10.1109/26.86568 ->
%   HTTP 404, and https://doi.org/10.1109/26.86568 -> "Error: DOI Not Found" (checked
%   2026-11-03). IEEE Xplore itself was not reachable from this sandbox, so the volume
%   cannot be settled from an identifier here; the entry above uses the fields the
%   resolvable DOI actually returns.

